.TH NUMERICS 2
.SH NAME
numerics \- general-purpose integration of explicit ordinary differential equations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "numerics.m";
numerics := load Numerics Numerics->PATH;
w := numerics->workspace(len state);
numerics->euler(w, rhs, t, h, state);
numerics->heun(w, rhs, t, h, state);
numerics->rk4(w, rhs, t, h, state);

tolerance := Numerics->Tolerance(1e-8, 1e-6, 1e-8, 0.25);
result := numerics->rkf45(w, rhs, tolerance, t, h, state);
result = numerics->adaptive(w, rhs, tolerance, t, tend, h, state);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Numerics
integrates a first-order initial-value problem
.I y'=f(t,y)
without knowing the meaning of the state vector.
The caller supplies a right-hand-side function that fills a derivative array.
.PP
.B workspace
allocates reusable Runge-Kutta scratch arrays for a state of the given size.
.B euler
advances one explicit Euler step.
.B heun
advances one improved-Euler step using the average of the initial and predicted
slopes.
.B rk4
advances one classical fourth-order Runge-Kutta step in place.
.B integrate
advances between two times using bounded steps and an exact final endpoint.
Backward integration is supported.
.PP
.B rkf45
attempts one embedded Fehlberg fourth/fifth-order step.  It measures the
componentwise error against
.IB absolute + relative*max(|y|,|ynew|) .
The returned
.B Stepresult
reports whether the step was accepted, the resulting time, normalized maximum
error, suggested next step, and number of right-hand-side evaluations.  State
is changed only after an accepted step.
.PP
.B adaptive
repeats RKF4(5) attempts to reach an exact final endpoint.  It observes the
minimum and maximum steps in the supplied
.B Tolerance
and raises an exception if the requested tolerance cannot be met at the
minimum step.  Forward and backward integration are supported.
.PP
The library does not impose positivity, conservation, event handling, units,
or model-specific tolerances.  Those policies belong to the caller.
.SH SOURCE
.B /module/numerics.m
.br
.B /appl/lib/numerics.b
.SH SEE ALSO
